# Build output
build/
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
*.list

# Signed images are derived from the binary -- regenerate, never commit.
*_signed.bin

# Generated by stedgeai / X-CUBE-AI from model_int8.tflite. Regenerate it (doc 4);
# committing it pins the output of one X-CUBE-AI version into the repo.
model/generated/

# Model artifacts land here via scripts/export-model.ps1.
#
# The .tflite and the generated headers are NOT committed: they are outputs of an
# EMaGerLib export and belong with that export.
model/*.tflite
model/emager_model_data.h
model/emager_model_params.h
model/emager_prototypes.h
model/emager_test_vectors.h
model/EXPORT_REPORT.md

# model_fp32.pt is the ONE exception worth keeping if you ship a firmware build:
# training is not seeded, so without it the weights behind a flashed binary are gone
# for good. It is ignored here because it is large; if you tag a release, attach it.
model/*.pt

# CubeMX output, generated locally into this folder (doc 3).
#
# Drivers/ and Middlewares/ are hundreds of megabytes of unmodified ST code, fully
# reproducible from the .ioc -- ignored.
#
# Core/ and the .ioc are NOT ignored: Core/ holds main.c with your USER CODE blocks
# (the integration code), and the .ioc IS the project definition. Losing either means
# the project cannot be rebuilt.
Drivers/
Middlewares/
cmake/
*.ioc.bak
.mxproject

# VS Code: keep the shared config, ignore what is machine- or extension-generated.
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/ipch/
.vscode/*.log

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
